1
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
We sigh whenever we're about to come to a standstill

2
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:24,460
Owarinaki tabi no tochuu tachidomarisouna toki

3
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
While moving on this endless journey.

4
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:30,710
Fukai tameiki kobosu bokura wa

5
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Everytime we lunge for it, it escapes and flies off.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,430
Tsukamikaketewa mata hanareteitta

7
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
But now, there's nothing to be afraid of

8
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:45,850
Demo ima wa mou nanimo osoreru koto wa nai

9
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
The powerful ties that bind our hearts

10
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:53,780
Kokoro wo tsunagu tsuyoi kizuna wa

11
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Will never come loose.

12
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:59,240
Keshite hodoke wa shinai sa

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
After a lifetime of searching, we finally arrived

14
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:08,960
Sagashitsuzukete tadoritsuita

15
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Here, where the period lies.

16
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:14,760
Kono basho de piriodo ni

17
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Let's change all our sorrow and rage to power.

18
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:24,060
Kanashimi ikari chikara ni kaete

19
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Destiny is right within our reach.

20
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:28,980
Unmei wa sugu soba ni

21
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:33,980
Shoot everyone except for Colonel Mustang!

22
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Upheavel in Central

23
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Upheavel in Central

24
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:52,710
By that,

25
00:01:53,130 --> 00:01:55,340
are you implying that the Madam may be shot as well?

26
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,640
Those are words I wanted to hear, but...

27
00:02:01,470 --> 00:02:02,550
I...

28
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:08,350
No, was my husband abandoned by his country?

29
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:13,270
Or perhaps, did he abandon me?

30
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:15,400
I can't say for sure.

31
00:02:17,690 --> 00:02:22,200
But you can rest assured that we'll insure your safety.

32
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:30,250
In order to prove after everything is over that what we are currently doing is not in the wrong.

33
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,420
Reinforcements!

34
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:38,170
Hurry!

35
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:39,970
Looks like you were saved.

36
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:43,930
Had we been soldiers from Briggs, you would have been dead.

37
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:44,680
What?!

38
00:02:48,470 --> 00:02:50,430
Long time no see, Colonel.

39
00:02:50,430 --> 00:02:52,020
Yeah. Good work.

40
00:02:52,560 --> 00:02:53,810
What's Lieutenant General Grumman up to?

41
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:55,980
He's dealing with the aftermath of the train explosion.

42
00:02:56,980 --> 00:03:01,610
Have you not mentioned to the Madam that her husband is currently missing?

43
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:02,660
I haven't.

44
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:05,450
It would be hard to move around if she were to pass out from the shock.

45
00:03:09,950 --> 00:03:12,250
They're gathering like ants.

46
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:14,330
You're too popular, Colonel.

47
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:15,590
You're telling me...

48
00:03:21,970 --> 00:03:23,590
You still haven't taken care of them?!

49
00:03:23,970 --> 00:03:25,260
What are they doing?!

50
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:26,760
There are only five enemies!

51
00:03:27,140 --> 00:03:28,640
They've increased in numbers!

52
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:30,980
Apparently, they're currently at least the size of a platoon!

53
00:03:32,390 --> 00:03:33,600
Our casualties?

54
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:36,610
59 injured, no deaths, sir!

55
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:39,230
None?

56
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:45,030
Damn them...

57
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:45,910
Are you alright?!

58
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:47,910
Just barely...

59
00:03:48,830 --> 00:03:53,790
The Flame Alchemist is the one who was devastating in Ishbal, right?

60
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:56,580
Am I the only one who feels like he's not as powerful as the rumors say?

61
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,290
Agreed.

62
00:03:58,290 --> 00:04:00,670
All I've been seeing from him are tiny explosion flames...

63
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:05,930
Jess! Parkie!

64
00:04:06,180 --> 00:04:08,300
Dammit! He got my eardrum!

65
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:09,600
What are the casualties?!

66
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,430
5 injured, no deaths!

67
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,560
We're lucky that none were killed.

68
00:04:19,440 --> 00:04:22,650
Both the hero of Ishbal and the "Hawk's Eye" are against us.

69
00:04:22,650 --> 00:04:25,530
It's strange that none of our men have died.

70
00:04:26,030 --> 00:04:27,070
It couldn't be...!

71
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,830
They really are!

72
00:04:34,830 --> 00:04:36,000
They're...!

73
00:04:36,750 --> 00:04:38,670
Going easy on us?!

74
00:04:38,670 --> 00:04:39,540
Yes.

75
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:42,710
There are quite a few casualties, but none have been killed so far.

76
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:46,010
Even the ones who were sniped were not hit in critical spots.

77
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,510
Mocking us like that...!

78
00:04:49,850 --> 00:04:52,220
Have the Demetri Squad and Kim Squad deployed as well!

79
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:55,480
Hurry up and make a stack of the corpses of Mustang's men right here!

80
00:04:56,770 --> 00:04:59,360
They still haven't captured Mustang?

81
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:02,190
What in the world is Brigadier General Clemin doing?!

82
00:05:02,190 --> 00:05:07,240
Apparently, they're only chipping at our forces without killing any of them.

83
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:10,620
There's no way they can keep up something that crafty for so long.

84
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:13,240
Colonel Mustang sure is soft.

85
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,910
Seriously.

86
00:05:14,910 --> 00:05:17,000
What the hell is he thinking?

87
00:05:18,290 --> 00:05:22,630
And the Central Army who can't even defeat him are even more inexperienced.

88
00:05:23,210 --> 00:05:25,130
It's almost like child's play.

89
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:26,260
What did you say?

90
00:05:27,550 --> 00:05:34,100
I've heard that headquarters was almost completely frozen by a single traitor.

91
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:40,770
Central has never been attacked by a large force since the country was established.

92
00:05:41,560 --> 00:05:44,900
This inexperience is its greatest weakness.

93
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:49,030
Good on the offensive, but absolutely terrible on the defensive.

94
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,160
What do you think?

95
00:05:52,580 --> 00:05:55,540
How about you put me in charge of the Central Army for a bit?

96
00:05:56,410 --> 00:05:58,910
Don't get too cocky, Armstrong!

97
00:05:59,670 --> 00:06:03,250
Do you think you're here right now because of your own ability?

98
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:06,920
You're only here so that we can control you.

99
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:11,220
We're aware that you and the soldiers at Briggs have a strong bond.

100
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:18,230
The fact that you're here is a powerful shackle on their wrists to prevent them from 		opposing us.

101
00:06:20,730 --> 00:06:23,770
You guys don't know anything about us!

102
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:29,950
I've told them beforehand to abandon me in the event of an emergency.

103
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:33,240
The law of Briggs is "Survival of the Fittest".

104
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:40,080
Even if I were to die here, they'd only shrug it off and say it happened because I was 	too weak.

105
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,580
They're a group that will move on without flinching.

106
00:06:44,090 --> 00:06:46,250
That's what it means to be a soldier at Briggs.

107
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:50,420
Don't you dare speak of the soldiers I raised without actually knowing them!

108
00:06:51,430 --> 00:06:55,550
They're currently exchanging fire with Colonel Mustang and the crew in the industrial area in the west district.

109
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:58,180
A lot of soldiers were sent to that area.

110
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:07,610
Let's do this.

111
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:09,740
Time to say goodbye to this cellar.

112
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:14,450
Give those cowards at Central a good bite in the windpipe!

113
00:07:18,290 --> 00:07:19,410
See? Here they come.

114
00:07:20,370 --> 00:07:24,250
Veterans who can put up a fight against the giant bears at Briggs.

115
00:07:25,170 --> 00:07:28,880
I wonder who'd win; them or those proud dolls of yours?

116
00:07:35,430 --> 00:07:36,260
Dammit!

117
00:07:42,270 --> 00:07:43,230
New forces?!

118
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:44,600
That's ridiculous!

119
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:45,650
Where did they come from?!

120
00:07:45,650 --> 00:07:48,070
They just suddenly appeared from within the city!

121
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:50,110
They're not magicians, dammit!

122
00:07:50,110 --> 00:07:51,440
You men go too!

123
00:07:53,070 --> 00:07:54,160
Enemy numbers?

124
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,280
Unconfirmed, sir!

125
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,830
But from their equipment, we can assume that they're from the north!

126
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:00,490
Briggs...?

127
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:06,170
From the Armstrong's mansion?

128
00:08:06,170 --> 00:08:06,830
Yeah.

129
00:08:07,630 --> 00:08:11,960
We snuck soldiers and weapons into the basement while the mansion was being repaired.

130
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:14,260
How big is the place, exactly?

131
00:08:14,340 --> 00:08:15,050
Charlie!

132
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:15,800
Give me some ammo!

133
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,550
Sorry, we're out too.

134
00:08:18,550 --> 00:08:20,260
This is bad...

135
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:22,390
What's taking the supply squad so long?

136
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:23,560
Don't tell me they were captured...

137
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:27,770
If things get really bad, desert me and run.

138
00:08:27,770 --> 00:08:28,610
Roger that!

139
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:32,820
Isn't this where you're supposed to say, "I'll follow you to the depths of hell"?

140
00:08:32,990 --> 00:08:35,030
Last thing I want to do is to commit double suicide with a guy.

141
00:08:35,030 --> 00:08:37,320
I've got a wife waiting for me at home, too.

142
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,700
Oh...

143
00:08:40,870 --> 00:08:42,120
...really?

144
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:50,210
Th-They've started using less bullets on us.

145
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:52,590
I'm assuming they're just about out of ammo.

146
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,720
Okay, let's wrap this up!

147
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:56,340
Gather everyone that's left!

148
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:06,100
Hey, Riza!

149
00:09:06,100 --> 00:09:07,900
You're late, Rebecca!

150
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:09,360
My bad, my bad!

151
00:09:09,360 --> 00:09:11,900
So for those of you who waited so patiently...

152
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:13,480
I've got a few gifts to hand out!

153
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,490
Amazing...

154
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:18,200
Not just ammo, but all this too?!

155
00:09:18,200 --> 00:09:20,370
Nice, Rebecca! I love you!

156
00:09:20,370 --> 00:09:21,160
Shut up!

157
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,620
Men without money have no right to hit on me!

158
00:09:25,870 --> 00:09:26,790
Here.

159
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:28,250
Yeah. Thanks.

160
00:09:29,120 --> 00:09:31,840
It's been a while, Colonel Mustang.

161
00:09:37,630 --> 00:09:41,430
Second Lieutenant Maria Ross,
 returning without permission, sir!

162
00:09:46,850 --> 00:09:49,100
Why aren't they rushing in?

163
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:53,480
They can't approach carelessly because we have the Flame Alchemist on our side!

164
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,950
But the Colonel can't go all out because we're in the middle of the city.

165
00:09:57,950 --> 00:09:58,950
Oh my.

166
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:02,950
I came to Central to find hot guys, but it seems like they're all nothing but cowards!

167
00:10:18,420 --> 00:10:19,300
Shit!

168
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:25,760
Tear-gas grenades from Xing,

169
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,270
packed with red peppers!

170
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:30,850
You got all of these from Xing?!

171
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:34,940
I hadn't heard that you were a part of the mission.

172
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,740
You procured all these weapons by yourself?

173
00:10:39,070 --> 00:10:41,280
Or was it on someone else's orders...

174
00:10:41,280 --> 00:10:43,870
Would you like to speak with him?

175
00:10:51,920 --> 00:10:52,960
We're good to go!

176
00:10:53,670 --> 00:10:54,460
Here.

177
00:10:55,130 --> 00:10:57,300
Some important person from Xing, perhaps?

178
00:10:59,010 --> 00:11:01,550
This is Roy Mustang, a colonel in the state military.

179
00:11:02,090 --> 00:11:03,590
I'm terribly grateful for-

180
00:11:05,050 --> 00:11:07,100
What are you acting all polite for?

181
00:11:08,310 --> 00:11:11,310
Come on, Colonel. Just chat like we always used to.

182
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,810
Eighty years at your service.

183
00:11:14,810 --> 00:11:17,360
Anything from underwear elastics to armored vehicles.

184
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:20,940
Just one call, and we'll have it delivered to you. Anytime, anywhere.

185
00:11:20,940 --> 00:11:23,570
Your friendly neighborhood Havoc General Store!

186
00:11:23,910 --> 00:11:25,070
Havoc!

187
00:11:26,990 --> 00:11:29,120
So, where's the money?

188
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:30,870
I'll pay up after I'm successful.

189
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:32,370
Keep it on my tab.

190
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,430
There's smoke rising from the city.

191
00:11:45,970 --> 00:11:47,760
I can faintly hear the sound of an alarm, also.

192
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:52,600
Looks like the Colonel and the men from Briggs have begun to make their move.

193
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:55,560
Central must be in a state of pandemonium right now.

194
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:01,780
Guess it's time to go.

195
00:12:01,780 --> 00:12:02,900
Yeah.

196
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:06,410
We've prepared the counter for the Nationwide Transmutation Circle,

197
00:12:06,410 --> 00:12:09,200
but it wouldn't hurt to stop it before it's activated.

198
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:13,910
He's basically just like how he was in the flask, but bigger.

199
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:16,790
If you destroy his container, he should perish.

200
00:12:19,210 --> 00:12:25,800
We'll... also be able to free the souls of the ones that are bound inside him.

201
00:12:28,010 --> 00:12:31,310
But how do we get to him?

202
00:12:31,810 --> 00:12:34,690
We're going to use the underground path I took with May in the past.

203
00:12:35,390 --> 00:12:39,690
There are tons of deadly chimera, but we should be able to get through with our current party.

204
00:12:40,070 --> 00:12:42,110
You stay here, Heinkel.

205
00:12:42,110 --> 00:12:43,110
Okay.

206
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:44,150
Sorry about this.

207
00:12:44,150 --> 00:12:45,200
Not your fault.

208
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:47,740
Doctor Marcoh, make sure the military doesn't find you.

209
00:12:48,320 --> 00:12:49,240
Yoki!

210
00:12:49,910 --> 00:12:51,740
You wait here too.

211
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:53,410
G-Gladly.

212
00:13:01,710 --> 00:13:02,500
Al.

213
00:13:03,340 --> 00:13:04,920
Yeah, Brother?

214
00:13:05,170 --> 00:13:09,430
I'm going to go out for a sec to beat the hell out of a certain bearded nuisance.

215
00:13:10,260 --> 00:13:11,560
Be careful.

216
00:13:12,010 --> 00:13:12,680
You got it.

217
00:13:33,790 --> 00:13:36,410
It seems like there's something going on...

218
00:13:36,410 --> 00:13:38,290
I'd hurry if I were you.

219
00:13:38,460 --> 00:13:43,300
Father should be revealing the secret to immortality soon.

220
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:44,460
I know that!

221
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:57,810
We're going to form a cordon here!

222
00:13:57,810 --> 00:14:01,310
Don't let Mustang's group or the Briggs soldiers past the line!

223
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:06,400
Have your soldiers retreat immediately!

224
00:14:07,070 --> 00:14:10,780
You all are the ones who took away my right to command Briggs.

225
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:12,030
You...!

226
00:14:12,030 --> 00:14:13,830
Do you think you're getting away with this?!

227
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:17,540
Let me redirect that question right back to you.

228
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:20,250
You've heard from that 'Father' guy, haven't you?

229
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:23,340
What you're going to sacrifice and what you're going to gain.

230
00:14:23,340 --> 00:14:25,670
Yes, of course.

231
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:29,170
We the chosen ones will climb to a new height,

232
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:31,890
and Amestris will change the world!

233
00:14:32,510 --> 00:14:35,850
Change must be accompanied by pain.

234
00:14:35,850 --> 00:14:37,850
Is it really that hard to understand?!

235
00:14:39,230 --> 00:14:41,600
You pigs are beyond all hope.

236
00:14:41,770 --> 00:14:42,270
What?

237
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:53,370
You cowards who hide in the rear lines and glance over the battlefield...

238
00:14:53,820 --> 00:14:58,870
...like to pass off 'pain' as if it were something noble, and proceed to make use of it.

239
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:01,120
Are you planning to turn traitor?!

240
00:15:01,710 --> 00:15:02,620
I don't know about that.

241
00:15:02,620 --> 00:15:06,670
I may have become a heroine instead, after everything's over.

242
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:07,800
However...!

243
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:12,260
I'm not as soft as the hero of Ishbal.

244
00:15:12,260 --> 00:15:13,550
W-Wait!

245
00:15:16,470 --> 00:15:17,310
What?!

246
00:15:20,430 --> 00:15:21,310
Sir!

247
00:15:40,410 --> 00:15:41,960
Major Armstrong!

248
00:15:42,370 --> 00:15:43,750
Sergeant Brosh.

249
00:15:44,290 --> 00:15:46,630
Don't you have the day off today?

250
00:15:46,630 --> 00:15:48,710
I rushed here after seeing smoke from my window.

251
00:15:49,170 --> 00:15:50,260
What happened?

252
00:15:51,010 --> 00:15:54,220
Colonel Mustang and his former men are holding the Führer President's wife hostage,

253
00:15:54,220 --> 00:15:57,970
and are currently on the run in the city.

254
00:15:57,970 --> 00:15:59,010
What?

255
00:15:59,010 --> 00:16:01,100
That coward!

256
00:16:01,100 --> 00:16:05,100
First, he kills the innocent Second Lieutenant Ross, and now he kidnaps the Madam?

257
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:07,940
He's a devil in the shape of a human!

258
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,360
Major!

259
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:20,040
In the meeting room at headquarters, Major General Armstrong killed Lieutenant General 	Gardner by...

260
00:16:21,040 --> 00:16:22,540
Shot to death?!

261
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:27,710
Okay.

262
00:16:27,710 --> 00:16:30,800
Seems like things are moving faster than I'd imagined.

263
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:33,470
I need to find the young master soon.

264
00:16:33,970 --> 00:16:39,390
However, I can't sense him because the giant flow of energy underground is interfering...

265
00:16:40,470 --> 00:16:41,310
Huh?

266
00:16:42,390 --> 00:16:46,900
It feels like the energy underground has spread more so than yesterday...

267
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,490
This won't do.

268
00:17:43,080 --> 00:17:47,120
The soldiers are gathered right in front of it, and we can't approach.

269
00:17:47,120 --> 00:17:50,000
It'll be a bit tough to force our way through.

270
00:17:53,750 --> 00:17:55,880
There's another entrance!

271
00:17:56,420 --> 00:17:58,010
Research Laboratory 3!

272
00:17:58,010 --> 00:18:01,890
Al and the Colonel have infiltrated there before and ended up fighting against the 	Homunculi!

273
00:18:09,810 --> 00:18:12,110
Three guards, huh?

274
00:18:12,110 --> 00:18:14,270
Okay, let's do this.

275
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:18,650
No no, this is the time for me to use my position.

276
00:18:19,360 --> 00:18:21,360
Soldiers!

277
00:18:22,370 --> 00:18:25,120
I'm Edward Elric, a State Alchemist!

278
00:18:25,290 --> 00:18:26,160
Huh?

279
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,790
A State Alchemist, sir?!

280
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,290
Please, help me!

281
00:18:29,290 --> 00:18:31,210
I'm being chased by Scar!

282
00:18:32,330 --> 00:18:34,000
He's a wanted man!

283
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:35,210
Freeze!

284
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:48,600
You're terrible.

285
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:49,980
Shut up, let's go.

286
00:18:53,020 --> 00:18:54,820
Yeah yeah, coming through.

287
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:57,780
I think it was around here...

288
00:19:00,030 --> 00:19:00,820
Here it is!

289
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,550
Should we split up?

290
00:19:19,550 --> 00:19:20,340
Yeah.

291
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,260
I'll go this way.

292
00:19:22,260 --> 00:19:24,930
Edward and Scar go the other way.

293
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:25,850
What?!

294
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:28,350
Why do I have to go with him?!

295
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:31,350
If you try to distribute strength alchemy-wise, this would be best.

296
00:19:31,980 --> 00:19:35,730
Besides, when the enemy sealed alchemy,

297
00:19:35,730 --> 00:19:38,980
Scar was able to use it but you couldn't do anything, right?

298
00:19:39,900 --> 00:19:42,740
Okay, then these two should go together.

299
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:44,240
What about the rest of us?

300
00:19:44,530 --> 00:19:47,830
I'm not your average Joe, so I'll be fine on my own.

301
00:19:48,910 --> 00:19:50,250
But, well...

302
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:56,750
I guess I'll take this lady from Xing as my bodyguard.

303
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:00,880
Okay, so if you see him,

304
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,970
give it your all to destroy him.

305
00:20:02,970 --> 00:20:04,090
Roger!

306
00:20:05,890 --> 00:20:08,470
Will you guys really be all right with just the two of you?

307
00:20:09,100 --> 00:20:11,100
Of course.

308
00:20:11,100 --> 00:20:15,560
Besides, old men prefer being alone with young women.

309
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:19,730
What a pervert.

310
00:20:19,730 --> 00:20:20,940
Let's go already.

311
00:20:37,540 --> 00:20:41,460
You need to find the Prince of Xing, right?

312
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:50,890
Go.

313
00:20:52,350 --> 00:20:53,770
Er, but...

314
00:20:54,230 --> 00:20:56,140
Don't worry about us.

315
00:20:57,350 --> 00:20:59,150
He means a lot to you, doesn't he?

316
00:21:10,370 --> 00:21:12,450
Thank you.

317
00:21:30,470 --> 00:21:32,470
Seriously, what pathetic fools!

318
00:21:33,010 --> 00:21:35,980
They can't even fight properly against those monkeys from Briggs?!

319
00:21:35,980 --> 00:21:37,310
Please, wait!

320
00:21:37,310 --> 00:21:39,690
We haven't finished experimenting with the soul attachment process yet!

321
00:21:39,850 --> 00:21:40,560
Shut it!

322
00:21:40,770 --> 00:21:42,610
When would be a better time to use them than now?!

323
00:21:46,490 --> 00:21:50,620
We've created so many philosopher's stones for situations like this!

324
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,590
Now, move!

325
00:22:03,590 --> 00:22:06,720
Devour those traitors!

326
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
The promise we never made

327
00:22:41,250 --> 00:22:46,210
Kawashita hazu no nai yakasoku ga

328
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
yet again

329
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,010
Kyou mo

330
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
tries to snatch our future away from us.

331
00:22:47,010 --> 00:22:51,840
Bokura no mirai wo ubaou to suru

332
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Why is it that we can't rejoice

333
00:22:53,470 --> 00:22:57,430
Hoshigatteita mono wo te ni shitemo

334
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
straight from the heart

335
00:22:57,430 --> 00:22:58,430
Sunao ni

336
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
when we obtain something we've always been after?

337
00:22:58,430 --> 00:23:03,400
Umaku waraenai nowa nazedarou

338
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
The overflowing tears aren't from feebleness or remorse.

339
00:23:04,060 --> 00:23:09,110
Afureru namida wo yowasa ya koukai ja nai

340
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
They're fragments born from agony.

341
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:13,910
Itami ga unda kakera de

342
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Of all the moments and destinies,

343
00:23:15,580 --> 00:23:18,950
Donna shunkan datte unmei datte

344
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
I realized there's one absolute certainty.

345
00:23:18,950 --> 00:23:27,710
Hitotsu dake tashika na mono ga aru to shitta

346
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Even if things get tough and I'm at my limit

347
00:23:27,710 --> 00:23:30,260
Genkai datte konnan datte

348
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
I refuse to give up.

349
00:23:30,260 --> 00:23:34,260
Akirametakunaiyo

350
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Please, don't let go.

351
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:39,140
Konomama hanasanaide

352
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
I can feel the warmth of your right hand

353
00:23:39,140 --> 00:23:46,980
Kataku nigirishimeta kimi no migite no nukumori

354
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
where it's tightly joined with my left.

355
00:23:46,980 --> 00:23:50,650
Koko ni arukara

356
00:23:59,330 --> 00:24:05,790
Souls that once dwelled inside humans now dwell inside puppets and are lurching forth.

357
00:24:06,750 --> 00:24:12,720
Although their appearances are deformed, their souls are indeed human.

358
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:18,220
Next time, Fullmetal Alchemist:

359
00:24:18,220 --> 00:24:22,250
Episode 51, The Immortal Legion.

360
00:24:18,240 --> 00:24:22,250
The Immortal Legion

361
00:24:22,600 --> 00:24:26,190
Should they be defeated, or should they be spared?
